{
  "name": "orkUI",
  "look": "office",
  "version": "0.23.0",
  "note": "The source of office/tokens.css (python tools/build_tokens.py). Dark only, soft and warm: the ground lifted and the ink softened so the screen does not glare (ink on the canvas about 13:1, not 16:1), and the greys warm in a half tint (each grey halfway between the full warm of 0.13.0 and the neutral grey of its own lightness). Still dark, and colour is still a signal, except the one ork green of the primary action: the warm tint belongs to the ground (the canvas, the panels, the table, the inks) and is never a mark; the table is a surface a step above the canvas, never a mark (decisions §53.5 of orkboard). The interface's text is IBM Plex Sans (body, caption, label); the pixel face is for titles, headings and buttons only; IBM Plex Mono stays the face of code, paths, diffs, logs and terminals. A long text read through (a spec, a document) lies on the paper in the reading ink (.ork-read): a step below full ink, about 10:1, so a page does not glare.",
